<report>
<title>Directly Standardized Rates</title>

<p>Rates are expressed per <in>units</in> of person time:</p>

<table>
<tr><th>Index events</th><th>Index PT</th><th>Index rate</th><th>Reference size</th><th>Weight</th></tr>
<block name="inputs"><tr><td><inu>idxy</inu></td><td><inu>idxn</inu></td><td><inu>idxr</inu></td><td><inu>refn</inu></td><td><inu>refw</inu></td></tr></block>
</table>
<br />
<table>
<tr><th>Index rate</th><th><ci>Exact <in>pc</in>% confidence interval</ci></th><th></th></tr>
<block name="cis"><tr><td><inu>idxr</inu></td><td><ci><inu>from</inu>  to  <inu>to</inu></ci></td><td><in>label</in></td></tr></block>
</table>

<p>Total events = <inu>events</inu><br />
Adjusted events = <inu>stde</inu></p>

<p>Crude rate = <inu>crude</inu><br />
Adjusted rate R = <inu>stdr</inu></p>

<p><u>Any rates (binomial model)</u><br />
Approximate standard error of R = <inu>ser_any</inu><br />
<ci>Approximate <in>pc</in>% confidence interval = <inu>from_any</inu> to <inu>to_any</inu></ci></p>

<p>Small rates (Poisson model)<br />
Approximate standard error of R = <inu>ser_small</inu><br />
<ci>Approximate <in>pc</in>% confidence interval = <inu>from_small</inu> to <inu>to_small</inu></ci><br />
<ci>Improved approximate (Dobson) <in>pc</in>% confidence interval = <inu>from_dobson</inu> to <inu>to_dobson</inu></ci></p>
</report>
